#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:76
msgid ""
"Served by the MLX vision engine, the one that runs multimodal models such as"
" Gemma 4. The drafter is validated against the target when the model loads."
msgstr ""
"Exécuté par le moteur de vision MLX pour les modèles multimodaux comme Gemma"
" 4. Le brouillon est validé par rapport à la cible au chargement."

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:79
msgid ":ref:`llama.cpp <llama_cpp_backend>`"
msgstr ":ref:`llama.cpp <llama_cpp_backend>`"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:80
msgid "``xllamacpp>=2026.6.9713``"
msgstr "``xllamacpp>=2026.6.9713``"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:81
msgid ""
"Translated into the ``draft-mtp`` speculative implementation. The drafter is"
" a single gguf published inside the target's own repository, so its "
"quantizations are its own (``BF16``, ``F16``, ``Q8_0`` for Gemma 4) and "
"independent of the target's. Earlier llama.cpp builds do not know the "
"``gemma4-assistant`` architecture and cannot load it."
msgstr ""
"Traduit en ``draft-mtp``. Le brouillon est un unique gguf du dépôt cible ; "
"ses quantifications (``BF16``, ``F16``, ``Q8_0`` pour Gemma 4) sont "
"indépendantes de celles de la cible. Les anciennes versions de llama.cpp ne "
"reconnaissent pas ``gemma4-assistant`` et ne peuvent pas le charger."

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:87
msgid ""
"Not supported by the Transformers engine: it runs its own continuous-"
"batching loop rather than ``generate()``, so there is nowhere to attach a "
"drafter."
msgstr ""
"Le moteur Transformers ne le prend pas en charge : sa propre boucle de "
"batching continu remplace ``generate()``, sans point de raccordement pour un"
" brouillon."

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:91
msgid "TRT-LLM"
msgstr "TRT-LLM"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:95
msgid ""
"Ordinary TRT-LLM replicas support NGram and Draft/Target speculative "
"decoding with ``tensorrt-llm==1.2.1`` on Linux/CUDA. The adapter supports "
"BF16 dense Qwen3 text models with TP=PP=CP=1. Xavier shared caching, native "
"P/D and Xavier P/D do not support speculation through this adapter; see "
":ref:`user_guide_pd_separation` for their supported configurations."
msgstr ""
"Les réplicas ordinaires TRT-LLM prennent en charge NGram et Draft/Target "
"avec ``tensorrt-llm==1.2.1`` sous Linux/CUDA. L’adaptateur prend en charge "
"les modèles de texte Qwen3 denses en BF16 avec TP=PP=CP=1. Le cache partagé "
"Xavier, P/D natif et P/D Xavier ne prennent pas en charge la spéculation via"
" cet adaptateur ; consultez :ref:`user_guide_pd_separation` pour leurs "
"configurations."

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:101
msgid ""
"NGram reuses token patterns from the prompt and generated text without "
"loading a draft model. For a workload with repeated text, pass the native "
"``speculative_config`` at launch:"
msgstr ""
"NGram réutilise les motifs de tokens du prompt et du texte généré sans "
"charger de modèle brouillon. Pour du texte répétitif, transmettez la "
"configuration native ``speculative_config`` au lancement :"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:131
msgid ""
"Draft/Target loads a separate draft model. Provide its local checkpoint path"
" with ``draft_model_path``; ``num_speculative_tokens`` maps to TRT's "
"``max_draft_len`` and defaults to ``3``. This counts draft tokens and "
"excludes the target's bonus token. The draft and target must have compatible"
" tokenizers and vocabularies, and both must be supported by TRT-LLM 1.2.1. "
"Use a smaller dense Qwen3 checkpoint for the draft when serving a larger "
"dense Qwen3 target. This mode does not require the Gemma-style paired "
"assistant or a shared KV cache."
msgstr ""
"Draft/Target charge un modèle brouillon distinct. Indiquez son checkpoint "
"local avec ``draft_model_path`` ; ``num_speculative_tokens`` correspond au "
"``max_draft_len`` de TRT et vaut ``3`` par défaut. Ce nombre exclut le token"
" bonus de la cible. Les deux modèles doivent avoir des tokenizers et "
"vocabulaires compatibles et être pris en charge par TRT-LLM 1.2.1. Utilisez "
"un checkpoint Qwen3 dense plus petit comme brouillon d’une cible Qwen3 dense"
" plus grande. Ce mode ne nécessite ni assistant associé de type Gemma ni "
"cache KV partagé."

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:148
msgid ""
"The examples require a compatible TRT-LLM environment. Change the model "
"sizes and draft path to checkpoints available on your worker. A draft "
"consumes additional GPU memory and compute, so it may reduce throughput at "
"high load."
msgstr ""
"Les exemples nécessitent un environnement TRT-LLM compatible. Adaptez les "
"tailles et le chemin du brouillon aux checkpoints de votre worker. Le "
"brouillon consomme davantage de mémoire GPU et de calcul et peut réduire le "
"débit sous forte charge."

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:152
msgid ""
"An explicit ``speculative_config`` takes precedence over "
"``draft_model_path`` and ``num_speculative_tokens``. The adapter defaults "
"``disable_overlap_scheduler=True`` when speculation is configured. Use "
"native TRT options only with combinations supported by the pinned runtime. "
"Other upstream methods, such as EAGLE3 and model-specific MTP, are not "
"validated by this Qwen3 adapter. ``enable_mtp=True`` only downloads a "
"drafter declared in the Xinference model spec; it does not enable MTP for an"
" arbitrary Qwen3 checkpoint."
msgstr ""
"Une ``speculative_config`` explicite prévaut sur ``draft_model_path`` et "
"``num_speculative_tokens``. En mode spéculatif, l’adaptateur définit par "
"défaut ``disable_overlap_scheduler=True``. Utilisez les options natives TRT "
"uniquement avec les combinaisons prises en charge par la version fixée. Cet "
"adaptateur Qwen3 n’a pas validé les autres méthodes upstream telles "
"qu’EAGLE3 et le MTP propre à certains modèles. ``enable_mtp=True`` "
"télécharge seulement le brouillon déclaré dans la spécification Xinference "
"et n’active pas le MTP pour un checkpoint Qwen3 quelconque."

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:161
msgid "When it pays off"
msgstr "Quand est-ce rentable ?"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:162
msgid ""
"Speculation is only worth it when a drafting step is cheap *relative to* a "
"target decoding step. The drafter is a small dense model whose cost does not"
" change with the target, so the ratio is what decides the outcome — and a "
"mixture-of-experts target can land on the wrong side of it, because only its"
" activated slice is read per token:"
msgstr ""
"La spéculation est utile seulement si un pas du brouillon est peu coûteux "
"*par rapport à* un pas de la cible. Le petit modèle dense brouillon a un "
"coût fixe, donc le rapport décide du résultat. Une cible à mélange d’experts"
" peut être défavorable, car seule sa partie activée est lue par token :"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:172
msgid "gemma-4 MLX, 4bit, M5 Pro"
msgstr "gemma-4 MLX, 4bit, M5 Pro"

